  "description": "In 1995, Jeff Bezos's parents put 245,573 dollars into Amazon. Here is what happened next.\n\nSources:\n- Fortune: Runs in the Family: Jeff Bezos's Parents Might Also Be Ridiculously Rich: https://fortune.com/2018/07/31/jeff-bezos-family-investment-amazon/\n- Fox News / Newser: Jeff Bezos' parents invested $245G, could be mindbogglingly rich: https://www.foxnews.com/tech/jeff-bezos-parents-invested-245g-could-be-mindbogglingly-rich\n- Wikipedia: Jeff Bezos: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Bezos\n\nFrom the cited pages: Jackie and Mike Bezos put $245,573 into Amazon in 1995, according to a prospectus two years later (Fortune); Jeff warned them how risky it was (Fortune); Mike Bezos, a Cuban immigrant and Jeff's stepfather (he adopted him in 1968, per Wikipedia), said they had saved a few pennies and were able to be angel investors (Fortune); Bloomberg estimated in 2018 that their stake could be worth almost $30 billion, a guess that depends on how many shares they still held (Fortune); in 2026 Jeff Bezos's net worth was about $284 billion per Bloomberg and Forbes (Wikipedia). Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #jeffbezos #amazon #howtheymakemoney",
